rows.en:
...Girls are scary{f:, you know.|, aren't they?}
You shouldn't read everything in the best possible light.
Especially in a club that's all girls, all kinds of things go on{f:.|, you know.}
Maybe you wouldn't understand, {c}{f:|}.
{f:You're not a girl, after all.|Maybe you've never been through anything like that.}
......
Oh well, never mind.
Okay, I'll end my story here.
Who's next?
What kind of story will they tell us...?{p}

There was no one behind her.
Not just behind her; there was no one in the lanes next to her either.
Hayashi was the only one in the pool...{p}

There was nothing there.
And the pulling, which had been so strong, suddenly stopped dead.
A dream...?{p}

But on Hayashi's ankle, there was a clear handprint.
When she saw it, Hayashi hurriedly got out of the pool, threw on her clothes, and went home.
On the way, she passed some of the club members, but she didn't say a word and left as if she were running away, they say.{p}

"Huh, I must've imagined it."
The meet's coming up, so I'm just a little oversensitive, that's all.
She told herself that and started swimming again.{p}

Hayashi couldn't stand their stares and ducked under the water.
She shut her eyes and stayed under as long as her breath would hold.
As long as her breath would hold... so two or three minutes at most, I guess.{p}

What {f:could|could} be in the locker Seto supposedly used, now?
Since it's off-limits, maybe there's nothing in it at all{f:?|?}
"What are you thinking so hard about, {c}{f:|}?"
Fukuzawa peered into {f:my|my} face.
"Hey, which locker are we opening next?"{p}

"Stop it, {c}{f:|}..."
She looked like she was about to cry.
Maybe I teased her too much.
"Sorry, that was a lie{f:.|.}
I don't think this is any cursed locker{f:.|.}
The whole cursed locker thing might just be something somebody made up.
Let's hurry, open the other lockers, and get back to the club room."{p}

Okay, {f:two to go|just two left}.
We've come this far, so there's nothing for it but to open every last one{f:.|.}
Which one should I open next...?{p}

"..."
There was nothing inside.
........................{p}

"{f:Hm|Huh}?
The door's {f:stuck|stuck}?"
The locker wouldn't budge, as if it were locked.{p}

"...{c}{f:|}, you can quit the act."
Fukuzawa frowned.
But it wasn't an act.{p}

"Fine, I'll open it!"
Fukuzawa reached out her hand.
And then...{p}

With the two of {f:us|us} pulling, the door came half open.
{f:But|But} it only opened for an instant.
That was because something inside slammed the locker shut{f:.|.}{p}

...Let's go back to the newspaper club.
And hear the sixth person's story{f:.|.}
We've come this far, there's no backing out now.
{f:We|We} walked in silence.{p}

When we got back to the newspaper club, the stuffy air greeted {f:us|us}.
{f:I|I} took a breath, then decided to hear the sixth story.
What kind of story was waiting for {f:me|me} this time, {f:I wonder|I wonder}...{p}

I just started running.
I had to get away.
Away from this cursed club room.{p}

"Gh... gah..."
My voice wouldn't come.
I can't breathe...{p}

Something like a cold hand touched my body.
But I couldn't turn around.
My neck was caught tight in the door.{p}

Then I noticed he'd already strode off ahead.
"W-wait, please."
I hurried after him.{p}
